WEBVTT

1
01:16:40.514 --> 01:16:45.914
We bless the family in the name of Jesus. We bless the dad and mom and the brothers and sisters.

2
01:16:45.914 --> 01:16:52.114
We commend them to you, Jesus, that there may be the peace of the Lord, that it may be within them.

3
01:16:52.114 --> 01:16:57.114
Strength and faith and peace and rest in the name of Jesus.

4
01:16:57.114 --> 01:17:00.514
We pray for provision and stability in this family.

5
01:17:00.514 --> 01:17:04.714
In the name of Jesus, we also pray for provision, economic provision.

6
01:17:04.714 --> 01:17:09.514
Lord, that you will provide, for the Lord is faithful in the name of Jesus.

7
01:17:09.514 --> 01:17:13.514
And we all say amen, amen and amen.

8
01:17:13.514 --> 01:17:15.514
Praise the Lord.

9
01:17:20.514 --> 01:17:23.514
Hallelujah, God is so good.

10
01:17:23.514 --> 01:17:27.514
Tim had asked me to share something about giving this morning.

11
01:17:27.514 --> 01:17:35.514
I prepared a piece, but you can turn it off again, because Tim didn't mention that he was going to do testimonies.

12
01:17:35.514 --> 01:17:38.514
And then I actually prefer to give a testimony myself.

13
01:17:38.514 --> 01:17:41.514
Before I knew God, I was a beggar.

14
01:17:41.514 --> 01:17:45.514
I always lacked money and had too little. I had debts everywhere.

15
01:17:45.514 --> 01:17:57.514
And then I discovered Jesus and I slowly began to learn how things in God's kingdom can work totally differently than in the world.

16
01:17:57.514 --> 01:18:01.514
And I learned about giving and I learned about tithing.

17
01:18:01.514 --> 01:18:07.514
And tithing was explained as giving 10% of everything that comes in.

18
01:18:07.514 --> 01:18:16.514
And I thought that is impossible. I am already short of so much money, how can I give 10% to God, give to the church?

19
01:18:16.514 --> 01:18:22.514
But I went to look it up in the Bible and I found enough verses where it was very clear.

20
01:18:22.514 --> 01:18:32.514
Where God clearly explained that if you invest your money in my kingdom, then I will ensure that you do not lack, but that it goes well with you.

21
01:18:32.514 --> 01:18:38.514
In fact, God said, challenge me, try it, and you will see.

22
01:18:38.514 --> 01:18:47.514
And I was going to do that because I had fallen so in love with Jesus right from the start that I thought yes, I want to live for him.

23
01:18:47.514 --> 01:18:51.514
So if he challenges me, I gladly accept that challenge.

24
01:18:51.514 --> 01:18:58.514
So I started giving 10% of what came in to the church.

25
01:18:59.514 --> 01:19:09.514
And I didn't talk about it at all, but I made sure that right from the first, when I received my salary, I would give my tithe first,

26
01:19:09.514 --> 01:19:15.514
then I could certainly not end up with no money left at the end of the month to do that.

27
01:19:16.514 --> 01:19:20.514
And that proved to be true.

28
01:19:21.514 --> 01:19:30.514
Instead of finding it even harder financially, things started to go easier and better.

29
01:19:30.514 --> 01:19:33.514
And slowly my debts disappeared.

30
01:19:33.514 --> 01:19:39.514
And I have been walking with God for 39 years now, and I can say, He is such a good Father.

31
01:19:40.514 --> 01:19:48.514
If you handle your finances His way, if you dare to trust Him with your money, if you take that challenge with Him,

32
01:19:48.514 --> 01:19:53.514
He will never disappoint you, He will never forsake you.

33
01:19:53.514 --> 01:19:58.514
Yes, you will go through seasons, you will go through difficulties and struggles.

34
01:19:58.514 --> 01:20:01.514
Also financially, but He takes care of you.

35
01:20:01.514 --> 01:20:07.514
He provides, His promise is so clear in that and so often repeated in the Bible.

36
01:20:07.514 --> 01:20:16.514
If you invest your money in His kingdom, He will always ensure that you have enough for yourself and enough to give away.

37
01:20:16.514 --> 01:20:20.514
So invest your money for God, for He is faithful.

38
01:20:26.514 --> 01:20:29.514
Rising God, are you ready for the Word of God?

39
01:20:29.514 --> 01:20:31.514
Hallelujah.

40
01:20:31.514 --> 01:20:34.514
Do you have your Bible with you? Show it for a moment.

41
01:20:34.514 --> 01:20:36.514
Wave it up high.

42
01:20:37.514 --> 01:20:44.514
Yes, yes, yes, we are building a culture where people bring their Bible with them.

43
01:20:44.514 --> 01:20:53.514
Did you see the message yesterday, in the app, where I said to just set an alarm, around noon, 12 o'clock?

44
01:20:53.514 --> 01:20:55.514
So just now, who saw that?

45
01:20:55.514 --> 01:21:01.514
Did everyone see it? So just now at 12 o'clock, everything, the whole church goes crazy.

46
01:21:01.514 --> 01:21:08.514
But I believe in the power of prayer. Amen.

47
01:21:10.514 --> 01:21:16.514
I have seen multiple things happen through prayer.

48
01:21:16.514 --> 01:21:27.514
About a year ago or so, someone moved into the street with a large statue and whatever.

49
01:21:27.514 --> 01:21:32.514
And I said to Joshua and Olivia, come, let's pray that this does not happen in our neighborhood.

50
01:21:32.514 --> 01:21:36.514
And what you think about it, I don't care.

51
01:21:36.514 --> 01:21:41.514
You can say that's coincidence, but we prayed for a month for that statue to go away and that statue was gone.

52
01:21:41.514 --> 01:21:44.514
So you can say, yes that's coincidence, I don't care.

53
01:21:44.514 --> 01:21:47.514
God can even work with coincidence, I really don't care.

54
01:21:47.514 --> 01:21:50.514
That statue is gone and that's what matters to me.

55
01:21:50.514 --> 01:21:56.514
And now that Halloween is coming, I'm just going to tell you my opinion.

56
01:21:56.514 --> 01:22:05.514
And I dare, filled with the Holy Spirit, to conclude that this is also spoken for the Lord.

57
01:22:05.514 --> 01:22:10.514
Halloween is a ridiculous holiday. It's just a ridiculous holiday.

58
01:22:10.514 --> 01:22:16.514
So don't participate if you've just come to repentance or you're coming from the world to peek here.

59
01:22:16.514 --> 01:22:20.514
And you're coming to see what people are here for. Listen, don't participate in Halloween.

60
01:22:20.514 --> 01:22:23.514
It causes occultism, there is a spiritual world.

61
01:22:23.514 --> 01:22:26.514
And do not underestimate that spiritual world.

62
01:22:26.514 --> 01:22:34.514
It causes fear, it causes depression, it is a bad, bad party.

63
01:22:34.514 --> 01:22:39.514
Now, as Christians, we do not have to say, ooooh demons, demons, scary, scary, scary.

64
01:22:39.514 --> 01:22:44.514
We do not have to say that, we do not have to continuously speak very badly.

65
01:22:44.514 --> 01:22:47.514
We have a victorious Lord, His name is Jesus.

66
01:22:47.514 --> 01:22:53.514
So we function in joy, for the joy of the Lord is your strength, hallelujah.

67
01:22:53.514 --> 01:22:58.514
So we do not always have to talk so grimly about life.

68
01:22:58.514 --> 01:23:06.514
But, when Halloween comes your way, I know what date that is, I don't really concern myself with it too much either.

69
01:23:06.514 --> 01:23:10.514
Then we can also say, yes but listen, we are not going to do that in my neighborhood.

70
01:23:10.514 --> 01:23:12.514
We are not going to do that in my street.

71
01:23:12.514 --> 01:23:19.514
So I would like to ask you, please set an alarm, six days at twelve o'clock.

72
01:23:19.514 --> 01:23:22.514
And then do it on Sunday at two o'clock, I don't care when.

73
01:23:22.514 --> 01:23:33.514
But the Bible does say, if multiple people desire something unanimously, so if they want something unanimously in the name of Jesus, then it will happen. Amen.

74
01:23:33.514 --> 01:23:37.514
So please, let's just take one minute like I do.

75
01:23:37.514 --> 01:23:41.514
At twelve o'clock my alarm goes off, then I look like this, I was at a football match yesterday.

76
01:23:41.514 --> 01:23:46.514
It goes like this, I look over there. Joshua is playing football, doing his best, then I walk away for a moment.

77
01:23:46.514 --> 01:23:48.514
And then I just go pray for one minute.

78
01:23:48.514 --> 01:23:53.514
Lord, I pray in the name of Jesus, that that whole organization in my neighborhood will lead to nothing.

79
01:23:53.514 --> 01:23:56.514
Lord, I break this down, this occultism, I do not want it in my neighborhood.

80
01:23:56.514 --> 01:23:59.514
Just one minute long, one minute goes by so quickly.

81
01:23:59.514 --> 01:24:06.514
But you know, when we pray for one minute with a few hundred people, we have no interest in Halloween in the camps.

82
01:24:06.514 --> 01:24:11.514
Whatever the result may be, you might still see a spider web or a fence somewhere.

83
01:24:14.514 --> 01:24:18.514
Your prayer has authority in the name of Jesus. Amen?

84
01:24:18.514 --> 01:24:20.514
All right, let's do it.

85
01:24:20.514 --> 01:24:26.514
If you have your Bible with you, go with me, because we are now arriving at the promise of what I was going to do.

86
01:24:26.514 --> 01:24:31.514
We are going to do a Bible study from the letter to the Ephesians.

87
01:24:31.514 --> 01:24:33.514
Everyone happy, of course?

88
01:24:34.514 --> 01:24:40.514
And I said a few months ago, I am curious, I was doubting a few months ago.

89
01:24:40.514 --> 01:24:44.514
Should I do Ephesians or Philippians?

90
01:24:44.514 --> 01:24:50.514
And then the conclusion was, let's do Ephesians first and then Philippians.

91
01:24:50.514 --> 01:24:53.514
Right? If you can't choose, do both.

92
01:24:54.514 --> 01:24:56.514
Praise the Lord.

93
01:24:56.514 --> 01:25:07.514
I don't know how long you have been coming to Open Church, but it has been a few years now that we as a church have been doing Bible studies on Sunday mornings.

94
01:25:07.514 --> 01:25:13.514
Because when you do Bible studies on Sunday mornings, you have the whole church, first of all.

95
01:25:13.514 --> 01:25:20.514
And secondly, you read through Scripture together and the subjects of Scripture present themselves.

96
01:25:20.514 --> 01:25:29.514
Instead of having to come up with subjects yourself, find a Bible verse for it, and then talk for thirty minutes.

97
01:25:29.514 --> 01:25:37.514
That's good, but much better is to go through the Bible and let the Bible dictate what we should discuss together.

98
01:25:37.514 --> 01:25:39.514
Is that a good idea?

99
01:25:39.514 --> 01:25:48.514
Well, we are going to do the letter to the Ephesians and I am really looking forward to it, because I find those letters of Paul amazing.

100
01:25:48.514 --> 01:25:50.514
Will you close our eyes?

101
01:25:50.514 --> 01:25:59.514
Dear Father in heaven, I thank you for your son Jesus Christ and I also thank you, Lord, for your congregation.

102
01:25:59.514 --> 01:26:04.514
Jesus is the head of the congregation and Jesus is wonderful.

103
01:26:04.514 --> 01:26:11.514
He is the head of the congregation, but the body of Jesus, the body of Jesus the congregation, is also wonderful.

104
01:26:11.514 --> 01:26:14.514
And we thank Jesus for the church.

105
01:26:14.514 --> 01:26:16.514
Truly, I thank Jesus for the church.

106
01:26:16.514 --> 01:26:22.514
It is through the church that I came to repentance, that there were people filled with God's Spirit,

107
01:26:22.514 --> 01:26:28.514
who were gracious and patient with me and could lead me to Jesus time and again.

108
01:26:28.514 --> 01:26:32.514
Through Jesus I am saved, by his blood I am forgiven, by his blood I am saved.

109
01:26:32.514 --> 01:26:38.514
But it is his body that is committed, so that the gospel is brought to all sinners.

110
01:26:38.514 --> 01:26:42.514
So we thank you, Jesus, for your congregation.

111
01:26:42.514 --> 01:26:48.514
And we bless us all that we will learn from this letter to the Ephesians, in Jesus' name. Amen?

112
01:26:48.514 --> 01:26:50.514
Amen.

113
01:26:50.514 --> 01:26:53.514
Ephesians chapter 1.

114
01:26:53.514 --> 01:26:55.514
Let us read together.

115
01:26:57.514 --> 01:27:02.514
What does it say at the beginning? This is a letter from Paul.

116
01:27:03.514 --> 01:27:08.514
I have received from God the task to be a messenger of Jesus Christ.

117
01:27:08.514 --> 01:27:15.514
I am writing this letter to the people in Ephesus who belong to God and who believe in Jesus Christ.

118
01:27:15.514 --> 01:27:27.514
I pray that God our Father will be good to you in everything and that you will be filled with the peace of God, our Father, and of the Lord Jesus Christ.

119
01:27:27.514 --> 01:27:30.514
Shall we say a hearty amen to that?

120
01:27:30.514 --> 01:27:32.514
Praise the Lord.

121
01:27:32.514 --> 01:27:42.514
What is always important when you are going to do a Bible study on a letter or a book is that you first discuss a few things together.

122
01:27:42.514 --> 01:27:46.514
You always discuss together who the author is?

123
01:27:46.514 --> 01:27:48.514
Who wrote that?

124
01:27:48.514 --> 01:27:50.514
Why did he write that?

125
01:27:50.514 --> 01:28:02.514
Why would you write a letter, like 2000 years ago, from one city, Rome, sent all the way by donkey, very quickly, hop, all the way to Ephesus?

126
01:28:02.514 --> 01:28:04.514
Do you know how far that is?

127
01:28:04.514 --> 01:28:06.514
Why would you do that?

128
01:28:06.514 --> 01:28:09.514
And who is that man? Who is Paul?

129
01:28:09.514 --> 01:28:11.514
And what has he done?

130
01:28:11.514 --> 01:28:18.514
So here it is important that when you read a letter, the authority of that letter is established.

131
01:28:18.514 --> 01:28:22.514
Paul says, I am Paul and I am writing this letter.

132
01:28:22.514 --> 01:28:25.514
And then Paul states what his credentials are.

133
01:28:25.514 --> 01:28:29.514
His credentials are, why? Who are you?

134
01:28:29.514 --> 01:28:31.514
What is your authority to do that?

135
01:28:31.514 --> 01:28:37.514
If someone just walks into the church here, whom we all do not know.

136
01:28:37.514 --> 01:28:39.514
And they just walk up here on the stage.

137
01:28:39.514 --> 01:28:42.514
And they just start talking about what we should do.

138
01:28:42.514 --> 01:28:44.514
We are going to tackle that.

139
01:28:44.514 --> 01:28:46.514
We will throw them out.

140
01:28:46.514 --> 01:28:48.514
Why? Who are you?

141
01:28:48.514 --> 01:28:51.514
Under what authority do you speak?

142
01:28:51.514 --> 01:28:58.514
For the Bible says, when an angel, when a messenger, or even a heavenly angel.

143
01:28:58.514 --> 01:29:01.514
Or even just a person in your life comes.

144
01:29:01.514 --> 01:29:07.514
And if they come speaking something other than the name of Jesus, cursed be he.

145
01:29:07.514 --> 01:29:11.514
So here is the first lesson, you should not just let anyone speak into your life.

146
01:29:11.514 --> 01:29:14.514
From whom do you take what advice?

147
01:29:14.514 --> 01:29:16.514
Who is allowed to speak in your life?

148
01:29:16.514 --> 01:29:25.514
Is it your neighbor with whatever he has, that he has so much influence that you start to behave like your neighbor?

149
01:29:25.514 --> 01:29:27.514
Does he have so much say in your life?

150
01:29:27.514 --> 01:29:31.514
Are they the people at your sports club with their opinions and their party life?

151
01:29:31.514 --> 01:29:34.514
That you think to yourself, oh what they have I would also like to have.

152
01:29:34.514 --> 01:29:37.514
That you start to behave according to what they do?

153
01:29:37.514 --> 01:29:44.514
Or is it the Word of God that may shape you and encourage you to holy behavior that is pleasing to the Father?

154
01:29:44.514 --> 01:29:49.514
Who is allowed to speak in your life?

155
01:29:49.514 --> 01:29:54.514
The people who are allowed to speak in my life is a very small group.

156
01:29:54.514 --> 01:29:59.514
Sorry, maybe you are not even in it at this moment.

157
01:29:59.514 --> 01:30:04.514
That sounds harsh, but that is because I must care for my soul.

158
01:30:04.514 --> 01:30:07.514
I have the responsibility for my soul.

159
01:30:07.514 --> 01:30:14.514
And so there are only a very small select group of people in my life who are allowed to speak into my life.

160
01:30:14.514 --> 01:30:16.514
As soon as I smell manipulation, I am gone.

161
01:30:16.514 --> 01:30:18.514
Even if I smell dominance, I'm out.

162
01:30:18.514 --> 01:30:21.514
Even if I smell false teaching, I'm out.

163
01:30:21.514 --> 01:30:23.514
For this is what the Bible says.

164
01:30:23.514 --> 01:30:25.514
Take good care of your own soul.

165
01:30:25.514 --> 01:30:31.514
So that only people may speak into your life who bring you closer to Jesus.

166
01:30:31.514 --> 01:30:33.514
Who make you more like Jesus.

167
01:30:33.514 --> 01:30:37.514
Be selective about who may speak to you.

168
01:30:37.514 --> 01:30:40.514
That is the first lesson from the letter to the Ephesians.

169
01:30:40.514 --> 01:30:42.514
In the first few words.

170
01:30:42.514 --> 01:30:45.514
Vanessa is one of those people who may speak to me.

171
01:30:45.514 --> 01:30:47.514
Above all, Jesus may speak to me.

172
01:30:47.514 --> 01:30:49.514
Paul may speak to me.

173
01:30:49.514 --> 01:30:51.514
And a few other people in this church.

174
01:30:51.514 --> 01:30:54.514
And I'm not going to name them all, because then we won't have time left.

175
01:30:54.514 --> 01:30:56.514
For there are many people in this church whom I really appreciate.

176
01:30:56.514 --> 01:30:58.514
This is a letter from Paul.

177
01:30:59.514 --> 01:31:04.514
He has received a task from God, it says there, to be a messenger of Jesus Christ.

178
01:31:04.514 --> 01:31:05.514
That is his credential.

179
01:31:05.514 --> 01:31:07.514
That is what he does.

180
01:31:07.514 --> 01:31:09.514
Paul is a messenger of God.

181
01:31:09.514 --> 01:31:11.514
Who is Paul?

182
01:31:11.514 --> 01:31:13.514
Who is Paul?

183
01:31:13.514 --> 01:31:19.514
Paul was born around the same time as Jesus Christ.

184
01:31:19.514 --> 01:31:22.514
About five AD, some people say.

185
01:31:22.514 --> 01:31:27.514
I don't really care if it's five AD, three BC, zero.

186
01:31:27.514 --> 01:31:28.514
That doesn't matter much.

187
01:31:28.514 --> 01:31:34.514
Let's say that Paul was born around the same timeframe as Jesus.

188
01:31:34.514 --> 01:31:38.514
Paul was born in the town of Tarsus.

189
01:31:38.514 --> 01:31:41.514
At that time, he was called Saul.

190
01:31:41.514 --> 01:31:47.514
And Saul from Tarsus was born at the same time as Jesus.

191
01:31:47.514 --> 01:31:49.514
About the same age.

192
01:31:49.514 --> 01:31:53.514
We don't know exactly how old, because those numbers are not in the Bible.

193
01:31:53.514 --> 01:31:55.514
We can speculate about that.

194
01:31:55.514 --> 01:31:58.514
You can speculate about that at a barbecue.

195
01:31:58.514 --> 01:32:01.514
Only we don't know for sure, and it doesn't really matter much.

196
01:32:01.514 --> 01:32:04.514
What does matter is the following.

197
01:32:04.514 --> 01:32:11.514
A few weeks ago, I said here on the podium, I had a sermon about Lech Aharai.

198
01:32:11.514 --> 01:32:13.514
I don't know if you can remember that.

199
01:32:13.514 --> 01:32:19.514
Namely, that God, no, that the people in the Jewish faith, they had something like...

200
01:32:19.514 --> 01:32:22.514
Everyone just follows the profession of his father.

201
01:32:22.514 --> 01:32:24.514
Even if you are a baker, you will become a baker.

202
01:32:24.514 --> 01:32:26.514
Even if your father is a baker, you will become a baker.

203
01:32:26.514 --> 01:32:28.514
Even if your father is a carpenter, you will become a carpenter.

204
01:32:28.514 --> 01:32:31.514
Even if your father is a fisherman, you will become a fisherman.

205
01:32:31.514 --> 01:32:36.514
Unless you are a very special boy.

206
01:32:36.514 --> 01:32:43.514
Unless you are one in a thousand of those boys who is extremely smart.

207
01:32:43.514 --> 01:32:46.514
Who has an extremely high IQ.

208
01:32:46.514 --> 01:32:51.514
Who has the understanding to explain the Scripture.

209
01:32:51.514 --> 01:32:54.514
Not only to explain, but to quote.

210
01:32:54.514 --> 01:32:58.514
The first five books of Moses, bam, just like that.

211
01:32:58.514 --> 01:33:02.514
Who can do that? No one in this room, I guarantee you.

212
01:33:02.514 --> 01:33:05.514
The first five books of Moses, quoting them completely.

213
01:33:05.514 --> 01:33:13.514
And if such a young man were found that he could do that, then eventually a rabbi would come.

214
01:33:13.514 --> 01:33:16.514
That was a professor of the Word of God.

215
01:33:16.514 --> 01:33:20.514
That was because the Word of God, the Logos, the Jews also knew that.

216
01:33:20.514 --> 01:33:23.514
Logos had a great significance for the Jews as well.

217
01:33:23.514 --> 01:33:27.514
Then a rabbi would know when such a boy was spotted.

218
01:33:27.514 --> 01:33:30.514
There is one like that, there is one like that.

219
01:33:30.514 --> 01:33:34.514
Then such a rabbi would say to such a boy, 'leg aharai.'

220
01:33:34.514 --> 01:33:39.514
That means, you are worth a lot.

221
01:33:39.514 --> 01:33:42.514
You must follow me.

222
01:33:42.514 --> 01:33:45.514
And that was, that happened very little.

223
01:33:45.514 --> 01:33:50.514
I don't know exactly what the number is, but it happened extremely little.

